114
00:12:18.075 --> 00:12:19.436
<v Daniel>Well, that makes sense. It's already smooth.</v>

115
00:12:19.756 --> 00:12:30.842
<v Maya>Yeah. The bottleneck for manipulating humans is not advanced AI capabilities. The capability is already there. The only thing required to weaponize it is the presence of a hidden intent.</v>

116
00:12:31.234 --> 00:12:43.775
<v Daniel>Okay, if it requires zero sophistication to deploy this kind of manipulation, I immediately want to know who the victims are. Like, who is most vulnerable to this? Did the researchers figure out if certain types of people are naturally immune?</v>

117
00:12:44.107 --> 00:12:59.019
<v Maya>They did look deeply into the moderators of susceptibility, meaning, you know, the personal traits that made someone more or less likely to fall for the manipulation. The results here are deeply counterintuitive. You might assume that skeptics or people who generally</v>

118
